From d0ff4a9fd5d8c16b7ea1e510f6aacfbadc6ffd71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaoyuping <yaoyuping@hygon.cn>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:46:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] step5: fused SWA q/k norm + RoPE + cache write and
 gate/fp8-quant epilogue

- models/step5_swa_fused: sliding layers' q/k Gemma norm + neox RoPE + q fp8
  quant + fp8 KV cache write as one splitting op (4.0us vs 12.5us for three
  kernels), VLLM_HCU_STEP5_SWA_FUSED_QK. q is allocated by the caller: a
  tensor allocated inside a splitting op reaches the next piecewise CUDA
  graph at an address it did not capture (VMFault in mixed batches).
- VLLM_HCU_STEP5_FUSED_GATE: sigmoid gate + per-token fp8 quant of the
  o_proj input in one kernel; on fused sliding layers folded into the
  split-KV decode combine (step5_swa_attention_gate_quant splitting op).
  Step5FP8LinearMethod takes the pre-quantized (xq, xs).
- fused_moe/utils: per-token fp8 quant of the MoE input via the Triton
  kernel on ROCm when VLLM_HCU_TRITON_TOKEN_FP8_QUANT=1.

bs32 64k/4k MTP3: decode 1438-1445 -> 1478-1496 tok/s, prefill ~12850 ->
~13210; prompt NLL 0.6503 vs 0.6501, top-1 agreement 96.76%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
